ralph/progress.txt:18879:  - For BE-0039-style operations stories, the four acceptance-criteria slots (success / validation failure / authorization failure / not-found behavior) map onto an unauthenticated single-method endpoint as: success = source returns a value, validation = wrong HTTP method, authorization = explicit "this endpoint is intentionally public" test that probes with and without an Authorization header, not-found = sentinel/missing-file path. Document this mapping in the test file comments so future readers do not look for a missing per-tenant authorization matrix on a global probe.
ralph/progress.txt:18890:- DefaultPolicy: 30-day RestoreWindow + 90-day ReapAfter for tenant resources (org/proj/env/svc); api_keys are terminal (Restorable=false) with 90-day ReapAfter for audit lookups; memberships are hard-deleted at write time (SupportsSoftDelete=false, ReapAfter=0).
