ralph/progress.txt:20377:  - Tests cover: TestJobRetryPolicyMatrixRoles (CapDeploy four-role allow Owner/Admin/Developer/CI ReasonAllowedByRole; Viewer/Support deny ReasonDeniedNoCapability), TestJobRetryPolicyRevokedAndExpiredKeys (disabled-principal short-circuit ReasonDeniedPrincipalDisabled even with Owner underlying role), TestJobRetryPolicyWrongOrganizationPrincipal (ALL six built-in roles including Support denied ReasonDeniedCrossTenant — CapDeploy is OUTSIDE the engine's CapRead+CapSupport cross-tenant exception, the load-bearing distinction from job.read's cross-tenant matrix), TestJobRetryPolicyProjectGrantContainment (admin-on-target allows; admin-on-target denies org-root and sibling-project; ci-on-target allows; viewer-on-target denies no-capability — pins both scope-containment and CapDeploy at the project-grant path), TestJobRetryPolicyEnvironmentGrantContainment (staging-Admin grant denies org-root and parent-project owned, allows staging-env-owned, denies production-env-owned, denies production env.write — pins the staging-never-widens-to-production rule for the mutating verb), TestJobRetryPolicyServiceGrantContainment (svcA-Admin grant denies org-root, parent-project, parent-env owned job rows; denies parent env.write and sibling service.update; denies sibling svc_b-owned job row; allows own svc_a-owned job row — full containment matrix at the deepest grant scope), TestJobRetryPolicyOrgGrantCapabilityMatrix (CI/Developer allow ReasonAllowedByGrant; Viewer/Support deny ReasonDeniedNoCapability via the org-grant path — pins the CapDeploy split with scope held constant), TestJobRetryPolicyForeignHomeOrgGrant (stolen-scoped-key guard: grant for orgA carried by orgB principal against orgB resource → ReasonDeniedNoCapability via the engine's `g.Scope.OrganizationID != principal.OrganizationID` filter).
ralph/progress.txt:20378:  - ralph/prd.json: BE-0279 passes:true with notes summarising the CapDeploy split + cross-tenant Support deny + bare-{job_id} owning-scope containment.
ralph/progress.txt:20388:- Remaining risks / follow-ups: BE-0277 (Implement POST /v1/jobs/{job_id}/retry) and BE-0278 (contract tests) still pending — the engine pin here is the authoritative contract until they land. The wire 404-vs-403 distinction for cross-tenant or unknown {job_id} (treat foreign-tenant or unknown-row {job_id} as not-found for non-Support roles, and ALSO not-found for Support because mutating cross-tenant must go through admin break-glass tooling, not the customer-facing retry verb) lives in the contract test for BE-0278 and is intentionally not pinned at the engine layer. Similarly, the job-state precondition (cannot retry a row already in a terminal succeeded state, can retry from failed/cancelled per the worker's idempotency contract) is a service-layer guard, not a policy-engine guard, and is pinned in the BE-0277 service-level tests when they land.
ralph/progress.txt:20390:  - Bare-{id} CapDeploy verb engine pins (job.retry BE-0279, future job.cancel BE-0282, future deployment-by-id mutate verbs like deployment.cancel-by-id / deployment.rollback-by-id at /v1/deployments/{deployment_id}/cancel / .../rollback) follow the EXACT SAME containment shape as the bare-{id} CapRead pin (job_read_byid BE-0276) with three mechanical differences. (1) The role matrix flips from six-row allow (CapRead) to four-row allow / two-row deny (CapDeploy) — Viewer and Support deny ReasonDeniedNoCapability in the role matrix and in the org-grant capability matrix. (2) The cross-tenant matrix flips Support from allow (ReasonAllowedBySupport via the CapRead+CapSupport exception) to deny (ReasonDeniedCrossTenant — CapDeploy is OUTSIDE the exception). (3) Project/env/service grant fixtures use RoleAdmin (or RoleCI for the explicit CI pin) instead of RoleViewer because Viewer doesn't hold CapDeploy and would deny on capability rather than scope — RoleAdmin keeps the test ANCHORED on scope containment, with one explicit "viewer on target project denies no capability" subtest in the project-grant suite to anchor on capability instead. Pattern locks in for BE-0282 (job.cancel) which is the IDENTICAL CapDeploy + bare-{id} story for the cancel verb — mechanical clone of this file by s/Retry/Cancel/ + s/retry/cancel/ + s/ActionJobRetry/ActionJobCancel/.
ralph/progress.txt:20392:  - The "stolen scoped key" pin (TestJobRetryPolicyForeignHomeOrgGrant) for CapDeploy verbs resolves to ReasonDeniedNoCapability (same as the CapRead by-id variant) because the engine's grant filter `g.Scope.OrganizationID != principal.OrganizationID` skips the foreign-org grant entirely BEFORE any capability check. The verdict is identical to BE-0276's foreign-home-org pin — the only thing that changes between CapRead and CapDeploy at this guard is the docstring framing (mutating-side-effect-at-Dokploy vs. cross-tenant-read-of-provisioning-history). The mechanical lesson: the foreign-home-org grant test is verbatim-clone-friendly across CapRead and CapDeploy bare-{id} variants; only the action constant, fixture id, and principal id need swapping.
