ralph/progress.txt:31611:- Remaining risks/follow-ups: none for BE-0431. BE-0432 (service_accounts tenant-isolation) is the natural next story — the BE-0426 organizations tenant-isolation template + BE-0429's composite-FK shape are the closer-fit references than the BE-0428 user template, because service_accounts has its own organization_id column (NOT a shared global identity).
ralph/progress.txt:31613:  - For a tenant-scoped table whose only customer-driven mutation is a single idempotent state change (here: Disable with COALESCE keeping the first disable timestamp), the BE-0427/BE-0429 invariants-file pattern still applies but the trigger dual-anchor assertion must drive through the **lifecycle mutation** (Disable) instead of a generic Update — created_at preserved, updated_at moves forward, plus the lifecycle field (disabled_at) is set. The idempotent-second-call semantics belong in the canonical CRUD test, not in the invariants file (the split rule).
ralph/progress.txt:31615:  - Forward-applicable to BE-0433/0434 (api_keys CRUD + tenant-isolation): api_keys has an Update path (rotate / revoke / patch metadata), so the invariants file should re-introduce the full Update-trigger dual-anchor test from the user/membership template alongside the rollback + nil-Tx guards; the secret-bearing nature of api_keys means the rollback test must additionally assert that no secret_hash needle leaks into post-rollback observable state.
