ralph/progress.txt:31804:- Added repository-layer tenant-isolation tests for the api_keys table at internal/controlplane/store/api_key_tenant_isolation_test.go.
ralph/progress.txt:31805:- 10 new t.Parallel tests covering: Get returns the right row across two tenants; byte-identical bystander snapshot proofs for UpdateMutable / Revoke / RotateCredential / TouchLastUsed (each with the api_keys_set_updated_at trigger anchor + lifecycle-column anchor); cross-tenant prefix-conflict proofs for Insert and RotateCredential (typed CodeConflict + bystander byte-identical + raw secret_hash probe + global-table-size probe + rolled-back-secret-needle absence); ListByOrganization isolation on disjoint counts (1/3/0) with non-overlap; ListByServiceAccount tenant-scoping on cross-tenant SA-id probes in both directions; and a five-method indistinguishability-and-redaction table test asserting cross-tenant vs unknown-id Code+Hint match across Get/UpdateMutable/Revoke/RotateCredential/TouchLastUsed plus a secret_hash needle redaction probe over each typed error's Error() / Message / Hint.
ralph/progress.txt:31811:  - api_keys.prefix is GLOBALLY UNIQUE (the apikey.go FindByPrefix doc-comment confirms this and the 0003_api_keys.up.sql `prefix text NOT NULL UNIQUE` row-level constraint pins it). The earlier patterns note hint that api_keys has "UNIQUE (organization_id, prefix)" is WRONG — there is no per-tenant-prefix uniqueness. So the BE-0432 service_accounts "two tenants share a slug" worst-case fixture has NO row-level analogue at api_keys; instead the load-bearing prefix tests anchor on the cross-tenant CONFLICT path (orgA tries to reuse orgB's existing prefix → CodeConflict + bystander byte-identical + rolled-back-secret absence).
ralph/progress.txt:31812:  - The secret-bearing extension specific to api_keys needs TWO probes that BE-0432 (service_accounts) does not: (a) a raw-SQL `assertRawSecretHashUnchanged` probe via `SELECT secret_hash FROM api_keys WHERE id = $1` that bypasses the typed Get/scanAPIKey path (a regression that scanned a non-secret column into the struct or skipped the field on Get would otherwise silently pass the struct snapshot while the underlying row drifted); (b) a `strings.Contains(err.Error(), secretHashNeedle)` redaction probe across yeCross.Error() / yeCross.Message / yeCross.Hint for every tenant-scoped mutation surface (a future error-formatter regression that embedded the row body would otherwise hand a peer tenant's credential to a probing caller).
ralph/progress.txt:31813:  - For the cross-tenant Insert-prefix-conflict test, the per-id probe alone is INSUFFICIENT to prove the rolled-back row did not land in some OTHER tenant's slot — the failing row's id is not known to the probe (the Insert never returned it). Add a `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM api_keys` global-table-size probe immediately after the conflicting Insert to catch a rolled-back row that survived in a partial form anywhere in the table.
ralph/progress.txt:31814:  - The `-race -count=1` full store package test surface against Postgres is currently NON-DETERMINISTIC under test ordering — the same code base produces a different (sometimes overlapping, sometimes disjoint) failure set on each run. Trustworthy verification for a new tenant-isolation story is `go test -race -count=1 -run 'TestNewStoryNamesOnly' ./internal/controlplane/store/` (targeted), NOT `go test -race -count=1 ./internal/controlplane/store/...` (whole package). The whole-package surface is useful for the carry-forward triage story but not for individual story verification.
ralph/progress.txt:31815:  - FindByPrefix is intentionally OMITTED from tenant-isolation tests because it has no caller-tenant parameter and prefix is globally unique. Document this absence in the test file's package-doc so a future reader does not look for a missing test (mirrors BE-0426's "tenant-root tables have no ListByParent" note).
