ralph/progress.txt:31967:## 2026-05-18 — BE-0436 Repository tenant isolation: api_key_scopes
ralph/progress.txt:31968:- Implemented `internal/controlplane/store/api_key_scope_tenant_isolation_test.go`: 10 integration tests proving every repository surface (Get / ListByAPIKey / ListByOrganization / UpdateScope / Delete) is keyed strictly by `(organization_id, id)` (or `(organization_id, api_key_id)` for ListByAPIKey) and that cross-tenant probes leave the bystander row byte-identical.
ralph/progress.txt:31970:  - `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryGetReturnsCorrectRowAcrossTenants` — two tenants, two keys, two distinct scope rows; Get returns each tenant's own row and the two reads do not overlap on id/org/api_key_id/scope text.
ralph/progress.txt:31971:  - `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryGetCrossTenantIsIndistinguishableFromUnknown` — cross-tenant scope id and unknown scope id render identical Code + Hint (no existence leak).
ralph/progress.txt:31973:  - `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryListByOrganizationCountsAreIsolated` — orgA owns 1 scope, orgB owns 3; each List call returns exactly its tenant's count, no overlap on scope id.
ralph/progress.txt:31974:  - `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryListByOrganizationIsolatesSharedScopeName` — both tenants carry a scope row with the SAME scope text on their own keys; each List returns only its own row.
ralph/progress.txt:31976:  - `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryUpdateScopeCrossTenantReturnsNotFound` — UpdateScope on another tenant's scope id surfaces typed NotFound AND leaves the bystander row byte-identical (no trigger fired).
ralph/progress.txt:31978:  - `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryDeleteCrossTenantReturnsNotFound` — Delete on another tenant's scope id surfaces typed NotFound AND leaves the bystander row byte-identical.
ralph/progress.txt:31979:  - `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryInsertSameScopeNameInTwoTenantsBothSucceed` — two tenants can each legitimately have a "projects:read" scope on their own respective keys (proves the UNIQUE (organization_id, api_key_id, scope) constraint is per-tenant, not global — the load-bearing reason the WHERE-filter byte-identical-bystander tests above are non-trivial).
ralph/progress.txt:31981:  - `internal/controlplane/store/api_key_scope_tenant_isolation_test.go` (new)
ralph/progress.txt:31995:  - The BE-0435 invariants file already covers `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryGetIsTenantScoped` / `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryListByAPIKeyIsTenantScoped` / `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryListByOrganizationIsTenantScoped` as plain "cross-tenant id returns the right shape" tests. The BE-0436 tenant-isolation file must NOT redeclare those names — `go vet` will catch it (the api_key_scope_tenant_isolation_test.go file ran into `TestAPIKeyScopeRepositoryListByAPIKeyIsTenantScoped` redeclaration on first compile). Future paired-CRUD/tenant-isolation stories should grep the sibling invariants file for `^func Test` before naming new tests.
ralph/progress.txt:31996:  - The byte-identical-bystander pattern for api_key_scopes carries TWO independent trigger anchors (`api_key_scopes_set_updated_at` and `api_key_scopes_bump_version`) — neither alone is sufficient, both together catch missing tenant predicates even when the column writes look correct. The `assertScopeByteIdentical` helper asserts both plus id/org/api_key_id/scope/created_at.
ralph/progress.txt:31997:  - The shared-scope-text fixture (both tenants carry a row with the SAME scope text on their OWN respective keys) is the load-bearing worst-case fixture for api_key_scopes tenant isolation: the (organization_id, api_key_id, scope) UNIQUE constraint allows it, so any List/Update/Delete regression that resolved its WHERE clause by scope text alone — or by id alone — would leak rather than fail with a duplicate-tuple error.
