ralph/progress.txt:32289:- Tests prove: Upsert INSERT branch returns the committed row (version=1, timestamps non-zero + byte-equal on fresh row, fields echoed verbatim, env/svc pointer round-trip); Upsert UPDATE branch on the scope-tuple conflict only mutates role + bumps version + refreshes updated_at + preserves created_at + ignores the caller-supplied id + keeps the existing principal_kind (cross-kind smuggling impossible); Upsert cross-tenant or unknown project_id surfaces typed apierr.Conflict via the composite FK to projects; Upsert duplicate primary-key id surfaces typed apierr.Conflict; DeleteByProjectExceptIDs with nil OR empty keepIDs clears all rows of (org, project) AND treats both forms identically; DeleteByProjectExceptIDs with keepIDs retains only the listed rows; DeleteByProjectExceptIDs is tenant-scoped (cross-tenant projectID cannot reach into another org's grants); ON DELETE CASCADE from projects removes grants when the parent project is hard-deleted; Upsert rolls back when the surrounding Write closure returns a non-nil error (proved via ListByProject — the only observation surface for a grant row); Upsert and DeleteByProjectExceptIDs nil-Tx guards render typed apierr.Internal, never a nil-pointer panic.
ralph/progress.txt:32325:## 2026-05-18 — BE-0440 Repository tenant isolation: project_grants
ralph/progress.txt:32326:- Added internal/controlplane/store/project_grant_tenant_isolation_test.go (8 integration tests + 4 file-scope helpers) covering the cross-tenant byte-identical-bystander invariant for the project_grants table.
ralph/progress.txt:32327:- Tests prove: ListByProject is keyed strictly by BOTH organization_id AND project_id (cross-tenant rows never appear in another tenant's response, principal_id can repeat across tenants without merging); cross-tenant projectID at ListByProject returns the SAME non-nil empty slice an unknown projectID under the prober's own tenant produces (cross-tenant probe is not a "does this projectID exist?" oracle); Upsert INSERT branch on orgA (with the SAME (principal_id, env, svc) scope tuple already owned by orgB on its OWN project) leaves orgB's row byte-identical across id, organization_id, project_id, principal_id, principal_kind, role, environment_id, service_id, version, created_at, updated_at — proving organization_id and project_id are inside the ON CONFLICT target, not just the WHERE clause; Upsert UPDATE branch on orgA (re-upserting orgA's shared-scope-tuple row with a fresh caller-supplied id AND a different role) bumps orgA's version and role + ignores the caller-id AND leaves orgB's identical-scope-tuple row byte-identical (including the trigger-bumped version + trigger-refreshed updated_at — either drifting would mean an UPDATE matched the peer); DeleteByProjectExceptIDs with nil keepIDs (unconditional-DELETE codepath) on orgA clears orgA's grants AND leaves orgB's grant byte-identical; DeleteByProjectExceptIDs with non-empty keepIDs (DELETE WHERE id NOT IN ANY codepath) on orgA keeps only the listed orgA ids AND leaves orgB's grant byte-identical EVEN THOUGH orgB's id is NOT in keepIDs and would have been eligible for deletion if the tenant predicate had been dropped; two tenants can legitimately each own a grant row with the SAME (principal_id, env, svc) scope tuple on their OWN projects without colliding, with environment_id and service_id pointers round-tripping non-nil through both Upserts — the per-tenant safety net that makes every byte-identical-bystander test above load-bearing.
ralph/progress.txt:32329:  - internal/controlplane/store/project_grant_tenant_isolation_test.go (new)
ralph/progress.txt:32345:  - The byte-identical-bystander helper for a table with nullable *string columns (environment_id, service_id on project_grants) needs a stringPtrEqual + fmtStringPtr pair so a failing assertion shows both nullability and value, side by side. api_key_scopes had no pointer columns and its helper was simpler — this is the first tenant-isolation file in store_test with a *string comparison and the pair-helper pattern will recur for environment_grants / service_grants / variables (which also have nullable scoping pointers).
ralph/progress.txt:32346:  - DeleteByProjectExceptIDs has TWO SQL codepaths (len(keepIDs)==0 -> unconditional DELETE; len>0 -> DELETE WHERE id NOT IN ANY). BOTH must have their own bystander test: the non-empty-keepIDs test is the load-bearing one because orgB's id is NOT in keepIDs, so a regression that dropped the tenant predicate would have deleted it through the "NOT IN ANY" branch. The empty-keep test alone would not have caught that regression.
ralph/progress.txt:32347:  - The shared-scope-tuple fixture (both tenants own a row with the SAME (principal_id, env, svc) tuple on their OWN projects) is the load-bearing case for Upsert bystander tests, NOT a degenerate case: organization_id and project_id are IN the ON CONFLICT target itself (not just the WHERE clause), so the per-tenant conflict-target safety net is what keeps the Upsert UPDATE branch from leaking across tenants. A regression that resolved the conflict by the scope tuple alone would have UPDATEd orgB's row through the trigger fire even with organization_id correctly in the SQL WHERE elsewhere.
ralph/progress.txt:32350:  - Cross-tenant probe indistinguishability for a list-read path: the projection is (len==0 + non-nil-slice + same shape under "unknown id in own tenant"), NOT the (Code, Hint) projection used by per-id Get paths. ListByProject does not surface a typed NotFound for an unknown projectID (it returns an empty slice), so the indistinguishability proof reduces to "empty non-nil slice across both probe shapes". The ProjectGrantReader's separate project-existence-check -> typed NotFound contract is proved by project_grant_test.go and intentionally NOT re-proved here.
ralph/progress.txt:32355:- Tests prove: Insert returns row at version=1 with database-assigned, byte-equal CreatedAt/UpdatedAt (no UPDATE trigger has fired yet) and DeletionScheduledAt=nil; round-trip GetByID returns the same row; Update bumps version by exactly +1, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves Kind / OrganizationID / ProjectID (the SET clause must touch slug/display_name only), and leaves DeletionScheduledAt nil on a live row; Update with matching If-Match succeeds (positive companion to the stale-If-Match conflict path already in environment_update_test.go); ScheduleDeletion bumps version by exactly +1, refreshes updated_at, preserves created_at, preserves identity fields (slug, display_name, kind) and the composite (organization_id, project_id) tenant key, and stamps DeletionScheduledAt at-or-after baseline.UpdatedAt; Insert inside a Write closure that returns a sentinel error rolls back — GetByID surfaces typed NotFound and ListByProject does not see the rolled-back row, so a half-written environment cannot survive an aborted audit/policy/quota step alongside it; Insert with a nil *store.Tx renders a typed apierr.Internal (the matrix-closer for env's nil-Tx guard coverage — Update and ScheduleDeletion nil-Tx guards already covered in environment_update_test.go and environment_delete_test.go).
ralph/progress.txt:32370:- Remaining risks/follow-ups: none for BE-0441. The next story in the priority order is BE-0442 (Repository tenant isolation: environments).
ralph/progress.txt:32379:## 2026-05-18 — BE-0442 Repository tenant isolation: environments
ralph/progress.txt:32380:- What was implemented: byte-identical-bystander tenant-isolation tests for the environments table at the repository layer (BE-0442). Ten new database-backed tests in a new file prove that every EnvironmentRepository method (GetByID / ListByProject / Update / ScheduleDeletion) carries organization_id as the FIRST SQL predicate ahead of any other identifier, that a cross-tenant probe is indistinguishable from an unknown id on Code AND Hint (existence-leak projection), and that a soft-deleted environment in one tenant never leaks into ANY read surface of another tenant. The bystander row remains byte-identical across every observable column — id, organization_id, project_id, slug, display_name, kind, version, created_at, updated_at, deletion_scheduled_at — with the BEFORE-UPDATE environments_set_updated_at trigger and the environments_bump_version trigger as the independent anchors that catch a momentary cross-tenant UPDATE match even when the column writes themselves happen to look correct.
ralph/progress.txt:32381:- Files changed: internal/controlplane/store/environment_tenant_isolation_test.go (new). PRD entry BE-0442.passes = true.
ralph/progress.txt:32383:- Results: BE-0442 acceptance criteria satisfied — (a) two organizations with overlapping-looking environment fixtures (shared "production" slug per tenant project), (b) principal-from-org-A cannot read/update/schedule-delete/list/infer org-B environments, (c) list queries return stable per-(org, project) counts without leaking other-tenant totals, (d) direct ID access AND parent-scoped access AND soft-deleted rows are all covered, (e) errors flow through the typed apierr surface — no JSON envelopes are constructed here (repository layer; envelope rendering lives at httpapi).
ralph/progress.txt:32386:  - The EnvironmentRepository's surface is a STRICT SUBSET of ProjectRepository's surface (no UpdateDisplayName, no Restore, no ListByOrganization, no CountByOrganization), so the BE-0438 project tenant-isolation template ports cleanly by SUBTRACTION — dropping four tests (UpdateDisplayName bystander, UpdateDisplayName cross-tenant, Restore bystander, Restore cross-tenant) and one helper assertion (the Restore-direction flip on deletion_scheduled_at, kept defensively anyway). Adding empty stubs that reference the missing methods would fail to compile — leave them out entirely.
ralph/progress.txt:32387:  - The ListByProject test surface is widened from the projects template's single ListByOrganization probe to a 3-case symmetry table (own empty project, cross-tenant project, unknown project) because the (org, project) tuple has more cross-product cells than (org) alone — each one must be a deterministic empty slice (NOT nil) AND indistinguishable from the others. The existing TestEnvironmentRepoListByProjectIsTenantScoped covers ONE leg; this file covers the OTHER two as a symmetry guard.
ralph/progress.txt:32391:- Codebase Patterns updated: yes — new top-level bullet documenting the BE-0442 environment tenant-isolation template (the project_tenant_isolation_test.go template MINUS UpdateDisplayName/Restore MINUS ListByOrganization/CountByOrganization, PLUS the Kind assertion, PLUS the 3-case ListByProject symmetry table, PLUS the projATuple lifting helper).
ralph/progress.txt:32396:- Tests prove: (a) Upsert INSERT branch returns the committed row with version=1, byte-equal CreatedAt/UpdatedAt (no UPDATE trigger has fired yet), all caller-supplied fields echoed verbatim, nil ServiceID stays nil; (b) Upsert INSERT with non-nil service_id round-trips the pointer to the exact text and accepts principal_kind="sa" alongside "usr"; (c) Upsert UPDATE branch on the scope-tuple conflict mutates ONLY role, bumps version via the environment_grants_bump_version trigger, refreshes updated_at via the environment_grants_set_updated_at trigger, preserves created_at, IGNORES the caller-supplied id (persisted id stays at baseline's id), preserves principal_kind (cross-kind smuggling impossible — the caller's "sa" does not stick when baseline is "usr"), and preserves the immutable identifiers (organization_id, environment_id, principal_id, service_id); (d) Upsert with cross-tenant environment_id surfaces typed apierr.Conflict via the MATCH SIMPLE composite FK (organization_id, environment_id) -> environments; (e) Upsert with unknown environment_id under the caller's tenant lands on the same typed Conflict for the same FK reason; (f) Upsert with duplicate primary key (different principal_id so the scope-tuple ON CONFLICT branch does NOT match) surfaces typed Conflict via the PRIMARY KEY (id) constraint; (g) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with nil keepIDs clears all grants of (org, env); (h) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with empty-slice keepIDs is identical to nil; (i) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs with a non-empty keepIDs keeps exactly the listed ids and drops every other row; (j) DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs is tenant-scoped — a cross-tenant environmentID under the caller's organization_id matches zero rows, leaving the other tenant's bystander grant byte-untouched and the caller's own grant intact; (k) ON DELETE CASCADE from environments removes every environment_grants row when the parent environments row is deleted directly (NOT via ScheduleDeletion which is a soft delete); (l) Upsert rolls back when the surrounding Write closure returns a non-nil error — the row does not surface at ListByEnvironment outside the rolled-back transaction (the only observation surface for grants); (m) nil-Tx guards on Upsert AND DeleteByEnvironmentExceptIDs render typed apierr.Internal — never a nil-pointer panic.
ralph/progress.txt:32412:- Remaining risks/follow-ups: none for BE-0443. The next story in the priority order is BE-0444 (Repository tenant isolation: environment_grants).
