ralph/progress.txt:32487:  - For services (BE-0446) the BE-0442 environment template extends with TWO additional projections vs. environments: (1) a Restore bystander test must exercise BOTH live-peer (nil) and soft-deleted-peer (non-nil) DeletionScheduledAt baselines on the bystander to catch both flip directions of an incorrect WHERE clause; a single state would silently pass a regression that only mis-handled the other direction. (2) The composite FK key extends to FOUR identity columns (id, organization_id, project_id, environment_id) — every GetByID-returns-correct-row assertion must verify all four anchors are distinct between the two tenants so a WHERE-on-id-only mistake collapses both lookups onto the same row.
