ralph/progress.txt:32546:  - The "leaf-grant tenant-isolation" template (BE-0448) collapses cleanly out of the BE-0444 env_grant template by SUBTRACTION: every leg that exercised the nullable *string scope pointer drops out. The TestUpsertSameScopeTupleInTwoTenantsBothSucceed test drops the `svcID := "svc_web"` fixture variable and the `&svcID` argument, and the corresponding assertion drops the dereferenced pointer comparison `*grantA.ServiceID == svcID`. The assertServiceGrantByteIdentical helper drops the stringPtrEqual branch and uses `after.ServiceID != baseline.ServiceID` directly. Forward-applicable to any future grant table whose parent IS the leaf of the hierarchy.
ralph/progress.txt:32548:  - The bystander byte-identity assertion's two trigger-anchored columns (Version and UpdatedAt) are the load-bearing leak channel for grant tables — direct column writes can look correct on a no-op or partial-tenant-leak path, but the BEFORE-UPDATE trigger ALWAYS refreshes updated_at and the bump trigger ALWAYS increments version on EVERY matched UPDATE, so either drifting on the bystander surface is independently sufficient to surface a missing tenant predicate. Asserting BOTH against the baseline (not just one) catches the case where a regression migrates one trigger but not the other.
ralph/progress.txt:32549:  - Naming: every *_tenant_isolation_test.go file under internal/controlplane/store/ shares the same `store_test` package, so file-scope helpers (`getServiceGrantFromListOrFail`, `assertServiceGrantByteIdentical`) MUST have unique names across the directory. Before adding a helper, grep `^func ` across siblings in the dir to prevent a same-package collision. The shared `stringPtrEqual` / `fmtStringPtr` helpers from project_grant_tenant_isolation_test.go are package-visible by design — if a future tenant-isolation test needs them, reuse verbatim; do not redeclare.
