ralph/progress.txt:33563:  - The BE-0462 (provisioning_jobs) -> BE-0464 (job_attempts) tenant-isolation gap-fill pair is structurally weaker than the BE-0458 (deployments) -> BE-0462 (provisioning_jobs) pair on the bystander byte-identity proof because job_attempts is APPEND-ONLY with the BEFORE UPDATE trigger rejecting every UPDATE outright. There is no Transition surface, no Cancel surface, no Update surface, so the "cross-tenant Transition silently UPDATEd a peer row" probe has no analogue here. The cross-tenant probes are confined to (a) Append's INSERT path possibly touching another tenant's rows (theoretically impossible with the composite FK in place, but the byte-identity bystander pinches off a regression in the trigger logic), (b) the GetByID / ListByJob predicate not crossing organization_id, and (c) the two cascade edges (parent job, parent organization).
ralph/progress.txt:33564:  - There is NO updated_at column on job_attempts (unlike provisioning_jobs / deployments / projects / services), so the trigger-managed-anchor invariant used in deployment_tenant_isolation_test.go's assertDeploymentByteIdentical and job_repository_tenant_isolation_test.go's assertJobByteIdentical does NOT apply here. assertJobAttemptByteIdentical compares created_at as the sole timestamp anchor (alongside started_at + finished_at as caller-supplied anchors that should remain caller-supplied verbatim under any well-formed regression). The pattern note for future append-only tables: if the table has no updated_at AND the BEFORE UPDATE trigger rejects all updates, the byte-identity bystander proof is mostly probing the trigger AND the predicate -- a regression that silently dropped the trigger would surface as a column rewrite the per-field assertJobAttemptByteIdentical catches.
ralph/progress.txt:33565:  - job_attempts has only ONE write surface (Append) and TWO read surfaces (GetByID, ListByJob), vs provisioning_jobs's FIVE write/read surfaces (Insert, Get, FindByIdempotencyKey, ListByOrganization, Transition + the worker-side ClaimNext). The cross-tenant test count drops from 8 (BE-0462) to 7 (BE-0464) accordingly -- the "Transition cross-tenant bystander byte-identity" test from BE-0462 has no analogue here.
ralph/progress.txt:33566:  - The job_attempt_repository_invariants_test.go file already exports a per-(org, job) counter (countJobAttemptRowsForJob) but NOT a per-org counter. The tenant-isolation file adds countJobAttemptRowsForOrg because the org-cascade test needs to probe "did orgB's TOTAL count change?" across multiple jobs, not just per-job. Forward-applicable to any future tenant-isolation story whose table has a per-parent counter in the invariants file but needs a per-org counter for the cascade-tenant-scope proof.
ralph/progress.txt:33567:  - firstAttemptID is a one-line list-diagnosis helper that names the first row's id (or "<empty>") in a list-assertion failure message. The same shape is informally used across other repo tests; centralising it in the tenant-isolation file (where the positive-direction-pair test relies on it) keeps the per-test bodies focused. Lightly reusable for future tenant-isolation stories whose List surface returns a slice of typed rows.
