ralph/progress.txt:34247:- Remaining risks: none for drift_findings tenant isolation. The two flaky service-quota concurrent tests are existing repo behaviour and not in scope for BE-0472.
ralph/progress.txt:34249:  - Helper-collision discipline at package store_test: `itoa` is defined in audit_repository_tenant_isolation_test.go and `itoaInt` is defined in idempotency_repository_tenant_isolation_test.go. New per-file integer-to-string helpers in store_test will collide. Reuse `itoa` (the audit-file form) when the test needs an integer-to-string for loop variables — adding a third top-level integer helper would fail compilation, and the package-level naming is already crowded.
ralph/progress.txt:34250:  - The drift_findings invariants file (BE-0471) DOES already cover the typed-not-found cross-tenant probes for GetByID and MarkResolved inline. BE-0472's value is the DEEPENING: bystander byte-identity loops with multi-row orgB pools, per-tenant row-count side-effect probes, and error-payload foreign-column-leak audits. A future agent reading the BE-0471 invariants file and concluding cross-tenant coverage was complete would miss the bystander-row-drift regression shape, which is invisible to a single-row inline `wantErrCode` assertion.
ralph/progress.txt:34251:  - The tenant-shared text shape probe for drift_findings is `dokploy_resource_id` (NOT NULL DEFAULT '' with NO UNIQUE constraint cross-tenant). Two tenants can carry the SAME `dokploy_resource_id` text — the table represents an `unmanaged_resource` whose Dokploy id is a non-key string surfaced into the operator-facing triage UI. The cross-tenant ListByOrganization probe seeds both tenants with the same `dokploy_resource_id` AND identical (kind, reason, level) tuples so the only thing distinguishing the rows is `organization_id`; a regression that filtered by any business column other than `organization_id` would surface here.
ralph/progress.txt:34252:  - The two-tenant fixture for drift_findings MUST seed per-tenant parent chains (project + environment + service). The optional resource legs are MATCH SIMPLE composite FKs to (organization_id, parent.id), so a single shared parent chain would not satisfy the cross-tenant probe shapes (a tenant cannot reference another tenant's parent — TestDriftFindingAppendCrossTenantParentIsConflict in the invariants file pins this). The seedTwoTenantDriftFindingFixture helper lands the per-tenant chain; tests opt into organization-level (every-leg-NULL) findings inline by writing struct literals that omit the leg fields.
ralph/progress.txt:34254:  - The global-count probe (`totalDriftFindingRows`) is the chokepoint that catches a rolled-back cross-tenant PK collision landing in some other tenant's slot. The per-tenant count alone cannot prove this because the failing row's `organization_id` is unknown to the per-tenant probe (it's the orgB bind value that the rollback discarded). This pattern is forward-applicable to ANY future tenant-isolation file whose surface includes a global PRIMARY KEY (no `ON CONFLICT` clause) — without the global-count probe the cross-tenant PK collision test is silently incomplete.
